From 8e8ca83b50e5d424eca8ebbe08df9647194433d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 03:16:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Text-form cognitive map input (MODEL.MAP_ENCODER.input_form
 text)

Ablation of the raster map representation on the try5 CE-only GT model:
the policy receives the cognitive map as text instead of a raster.

- text_map_encoder.py: map_text_entities() serialises a cached map (grid +
  direction_vectors, downsampled by text_scale, 2 -> 50x50) into one
  sentence per nonzero category ("region hallway: 23 cells, center (14,27),
  extent 6x11") plus one heading sentence; MapTextTokenizer gives BERT
  word-piece ids ([CLS] ... [SEP], pad 1, <= 64); TextMapEncoder encodes
  each sentence with a frozen deepcopy of the policy's own instruction
  encoder (embeddings + lang_encoder, kept in eval mode), projects the
  first-token vector with a trainable Linear+LayerNorm, appends the usual
  metadata token (start pose; direction slots zero) and returns masked
  variable-length map tokens for the unchanged GraphMapCrossAttention.
- policy.py: input_form text builds TextMapEncoder instead of
  EmbeddingGridMapEncoder (no category projection, spatial tokenizer or map
  token transformer exist in that mode); map_encoding accepts
  map_text_ids / map_text_masks; coordinate_fusion is refused with text.
- ss_trainer_ETP_PriorGT.py: _build_cognitive_maps attaches map_text_ids
  once per episode; _prepare_map_inputs batches them (pad to the longest
  entity list) and calls the text encoder; map_ablation must be none.
- default.py: MAP_ENCODER.input_form ("raster" default) and text_scale (2).
- run_dagger_coord_fusion.sh: INPUT_FORM knob (-> eval_args.txt, run
  suffix _text) and a gt_legacy arm (18600 recipe: 440000 pretrain,
  gt.legacy.r1p5.direction5.v1, meters_per_unit 1.0).
- tests/test_text_map_encoder.py: serialisation, tokeniser, shapes/masks,
  frozen-vs-trainable split.

Default raster path untouched: with input_form raster no new module is
instantiated and no new code runs, so existing checkpoints load and
evaluate as before (their eval_args.txt carry no input_form).

